WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.670
Each May, Buddhist homes and temples
glow with lanterns and lights for Wesak.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:10.760
Families clean and decorate their homes,
make offerings and listen to teaching.

3
00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:15.390
And in February, many Mahayana
Buddhists hold a festival for a death:

4
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.360
the day the Buddha died, aged 80.

5
00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:22.710
Why would anyone make a festival
out of the day their teacher died?

6
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.090
In this mission, you'll find out what
Buddhists remember at their biggest festivals,

7
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.720
and how they keep them.

8
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.550
Then you'll weigh up whether festivals
still matter for Buddhists in Britain today.

9
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.000
Your mission: find out why Buddhists
would hold a festival to remember the day

10
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.240
their teacher died.
